\name{cellucid_camera_path_play}
\alias{cellucid_camera_path_play}
\title{Play the camera path}
\usage{
cellucid_camera_path_play(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Play the camera path in the selected view from its first keyframe, as Play does; answers when it ends or camera_path_stop or the person's Stop stops it (the camera stays where it stopped; a looping path plays on until stopped, by camera_path_stop or the person's Stop of this turn), with ended "end", "stopped", "looping" or "reduced-motion": the person's system asks for reduced motion, so the camera went to the last keyframe without moving (seconds: how long it moved, 0 when at once); nothing played, so never describe a film that ran.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{camera-path.play} (Camera path). It changes what the viewer shows: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{camera}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_camera_path_play(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
